s1-p17 = prose (cons "**Language, history, and inherited knowledge.** Human knowledge is inherited through language. Words, their uses, and their etymological histories transmit distinctions that no present speaker originated alone. Taken across its meanings and history, a word opens onto the intellectual activity of the human superorganism: generations of interpretation, communication, and action remain implicated in its present use. That inheritance is distributed among participants and artifacts; it is not a stock of facts simultaneously available to a single knower. Language belongs inside the history under investigation, not in a fixed dictionary supplied before the investigation begins." nil)
